Z||000000||Nyte||07-11-2001||03:38 PM||||Any tips on getting rid of an '84 Fiero with electrical engine problems (runs good if you jiggle wires around) and no battery in Orange County, California?  The thing has good body panels and excelent interior with a non-cracked dash, new seats, and all around neatness.  One thing, it's missing the left fender.  After it started running strange my dad and I pretty much didn't want to mess with it, in favor of a more reliable car, it was just for temporary transportation anyways.  <B>I don't want <I>too</I> much for it.</B><P>      <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/zfieropass.jpg">      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/fierodash.jpg">     <P>     <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/fieroseats.jpg">     <P>     <IMG SRC="http://sndfr.homestead.com/files/fierofender.jpg">     <P>------------------<BR><B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B><BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><P>"Damned '84 econo coupes!  Why didn't you guys tell me this BEFORE I bought the dang thing!"<p>[This message has been edited by Nyte (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||6
